<h2>About BlessBoard</h2>
<p>BlessBoard provides church software tools including public websites, member portals, branch administration, and multi-branch headquarters features. BlessBoard is developed and supported using GetPro technology.</p>

<h2>Platform website</h2>
<p>blessboard.com helps visitors find a congregation, learn about the platform, and contact BlessBoard administrators. Use the site lawfully and do not attempt to disrupt directory, contact, or sign-in features.</p>

<h2>Church sites and accounts</h2>
<p>Each congregation manages its own branch site content, member access, and administrator accounts. Feature availability may depend on that organization’s plan and operational status on the platform.</p>
<p>Access to a church member portal or administrator area requires credentials issued or approved by that church. BlessBoard platform administrators provision organizations; day-to-day membership decisions remain with each congregation.</p>

<h2>Your responsibilities</h2>
<ul>
  <li>Keep your sign-in details private and notify your church administrators if you suspect unauthorized access to a church account.</li>
  <li>Do not use another person’s account or attempt to access congregations you are not authorized to administer.</li>
  <li>Contact your church first for questions about sermons, events, giving, membership, or local content published on its site.</li>
</ul>

<h2>Service changes</h2>
<p>BlessBoard may update platform features, availability, or these informational pages as the product evolves. Material changes affecting your church’s use are communicated through platform administrators and church leadership channels.</p>

<h2>Questions</h2>
<p>Platform terms questions: <a href="/contact">Contact BlessBoard</a>. See also <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> and <a href="/security">Security and Data Information</a>.</p>
